    <sys:String x:Key="Lang.Log.SwitchSplit">Per-channel files detected — switched to split-channel input.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.ResetDefaults">Reset every encode parameter to the official defaults</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.LoadSettings">Load encode parameters from a saved profile</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.SaveSettings">Save the current encode parameters to the profile</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.SaveSettingsAs">Save the current encode parameters as a new profile file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.SingleMode">Use one multichannel WAV (up to 7.1). Channels are reordered automatically from the dwChannelMask to the order the DTS engine expects</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.SplitMode">One mono WAV per channel. Import any single track: its channel is recognized and the other channels with the same name in the folder are imported automatically</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.AutoDetectLayout">When importing, switch automatically to the best-matching channel layout using the channel tags in the file names (L/FL/Left, Ls/SL, Lsr/BL, LFE/Sub/SW…) or the WAV channel mask</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Layout">Channel layout to encode; follows the imported tracks when “Auto-detect channel layout” is on</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.ClearAll">Clear all imported tracks</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.SpeakerLayout">Speaker positions of the current channel layout</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.SingleFile">Path of the multichannel WAV — you can also drag the file onto this area</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Browse">Browse for a file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.BrowseChannel">Pick any channel file: it is placed into the matching row and the rest of its group is imported too</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.BrowseSave">Choose where to save the output file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.BrowseFolder">Browse for a folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.ChannelAliases">Channel tags recognized in file names (case-insensitive):</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.ChannelFile">Mono WAV for this channel. Drag it in or click Browse…; names such as Title_L.wav, Title.FL.wav, Title-Left.wav are recognized</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Output">Encoder output path (.dtshd / .cpt / .wav depending on the destination format)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.DestFormat">Destination format: Blu-ray / BD secondary audio / DVD / DTS Music Disc / digital delivery</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.StreamType">Stream type, e.g. DTS-HD Master Audio (lossless) or DTS-HD High Resolution</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.EncodeType">Encode type</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.SampleRate">Sample rate; synced from the input WAV automatically</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.BitWidth">Bit depth (16 / 24 bit); synced from the input WAV automatically</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.CoreBitRate">Bit rate of the backward-compatible DTS core, in kbps</sys:String>
